{"duration_api_ms":30501,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"85608b6a-bf68-430f-9e0b-83c1884a759d","total_cost_usd":1.0296678000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":112450,"cache_read_input_tokens":386859,"output_tokens":2634,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":682},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":112450,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":689,"cache_read_input_tokens":194187,"cache_creation_input_tokens":80475,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":80475},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":2634,"cacheReadInputTokens":386859,"cacheCreationInputTokens":112450,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0296678000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":682,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the labels to `labels/coder-1.json` (codebook 0.4, coder slot 1). There is one row, for the parent-notification topic (`egi-draft-a1v2`), and I put it on **rung 2: \"Forbid rules that require schools to tell parents.\"**\n\n- **The vote:** Quirk-Silva voted Aye when the Assembly concurred in the Senate's amendments to AB 1955 (2023-2024) on 2024-06-27. That was the Assembly's final vote on the chaptered text, and it passed 61-16. It is from her current term.\n- **What the bill does:** Section 220.5 bars schools and boards from enacting or enforcing any rule that would require staff to disclose a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent. That matches rung 2.\n- **Why not rung 1:** the bill doesn't require staff to keep the information from parents. Section 220.3 only says staff can't be *required* to disclose.\n- **Not near-unanimous:** 16 of 77 voted No, about 21%.\n- **Sources and quotes:** the chair rests on both pages of that one vote, the vote page and the bill text. Because they are one record, the evidence tier comes out single-source. I listed no missing sources and no quotes, since nothing here is in her own words.\n\nOne judgement call a reviewer might question: I treated AB 1955 as a single-subject bill, so a vote on final passage can seat a chair. Besides the disclosure ban, it also has the state department of education develop resources for families of LGBTQ pupils and protects employees from retaliation. I read all three as one subject, pupil rights for LGBTQ students; if a reviewer reads the bill as multi-subject, the vote proves a side but not a rung, and the row would go blank as `direction-only`.\n\nSeparately, the GitHub connector failed to connect this session, and seven claude.ai connectors (Benevity, Candid, Canva, Figma, Givebutter, Harvey, WorkOS) need authorizing in claude.ai settings. None of them was needed for this task.","ttft_ms":13576,"type":"result","duration_ms":34564,"uuid":"7d8a560a-718e-4520-84fe-046ddda6102f","ttft_stream_ms":7709,"time_to_request_ms":1349,"first_content_frame_ms":7709,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
